WEBVTT

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.269
Hey, wanna play a match?

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:48.441
Ten minutes.

00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:55.407
"Winners and Losers"

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.704
Hirari, I've lost my confidence.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.330
I know.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.874
Middle schoolers these
days are seriously strong.

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:06.668
They're way too good.

00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:09.838
Well, since we managed to survive,

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:12.257
let's reach for the top, bro!

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:13.633
Yeah, bro!

00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:19.681
Of course, we're only here
because of Otori-<i>kun</i>.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.229
What's up, Tenjin?

00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:30.734
You're kidding.

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:37.782
That midget's playing with Tokugawa!

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:43.872
That's the middle schooler
who beat Matsudaira.

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:49.711
Here I come.

00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:53.131
Drive B!

00:02:56.343 --> 00:02:59.179
Tokugawa's being pressured.

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:01.306
You can't be serious.

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:09.356
Ultra Great Delicious Mountain Storm!

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:25.538
What's up with those crazy moves?

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:30.085
What's going on?

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:33.213
Look at Oni's strings.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.797
Huh?

00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:40.387
That's not his two string racquet.
He's playing for real.

00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:41.971
I'm getting excited!

00:03:44.432 --> 00:03:48.269
That's a full string Black Jack Knife.

00:03:48.812 --> 00:03:51.940
That'll take both of the kid's arms off!

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.651
Black Jack Knife!

00:03:54.651 --> 00:03:56.194
This is it!

00:03:56.194 --> 00:03:59.739
My Super Ultra Great Delicious
Mountain Storm's next!

00:04:00.407 --> 00:04:02.283
How's that different from the last one?

00:04:02.283 --> 00:04:05.120
It's got a "Super" at the front!

00:04:06.121 --> 00:04:11.042
Super Ultra Great Delicious
Mountain Storm!

00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:17.215
I had a feeling we would
play against each other.

00:04:18.425 --> 00:04:20.927
Really? Thanks.

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:31.229
Cool Drive!

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.198
What's this?

00:04:42.657 --> 00:04:47.871
Court 1's Tokugawa and the fearsome Oni

00:04:47.871 --> 00:04:51.082
both lost a point to some middle schoolers.

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:56.338
They've completely lost
control of the match.

00:04:56.338 --> 00:04:58.256
Lost control?

00:04:58.256 --> 00:05:00.216
To middle schoolers?

00:05:00.842 --> 00:05:02.010
That's ridiculous.

00:05:02.761 --> 00:05:04.220
What? But...

00:05:04.596 --> 00:05:06.222
Look carefully.

00:05:06.222 --> 00:05:09.684
You can tell they're not really trying.

00:05:09.684 --> 00:05:11.478
As proof of that,

00:05:11.936 --> 00:05:16.358
even with such an aggressive
attack, the middle schoolers

00:05:16.358 --> 00:05:18.360
have only won a couple points.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.279
In contrast to their heavy
breathing and sweat...

00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:25.658
Tokugawa and Oni might be sweating,

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:28.328
but they're breathing normally.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:33.124
They're playing coolly and calmly.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:36.586
Seishun Academy's Ryoma Echizen

00:05:36.586 --> 00:05:39.255
and Shitenhoji's Kintaro Toyama.

00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:42.676
They're considered two first
years who will be the mainstays

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:44.469
of the next generation,

00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:48.598
but I wonder how those two
high schoolers view them.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.768
I can't tear my eyes away.

00:05:52.435 --> 00:05:57.440
You must keep a close
eye on the main court.

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:01.945
Don't tell me you've forgotten
about that report.

00:06:01.945 --> 00:06:03.488
Oh, right.

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.786
Game and match, Shiraishi.

00:06:09.786 --> 00:06:10.829
Seven-three.

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:13.039
Amazing.

00:06:13.456 --> 00:06:18.545
Shitenhoji's so-called Bible,
Kuranosuke Shiraishi-<i>san</i>.

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:22.132
He plays with perfect efficiency,
wasting nothing.

00:06:22.799 --> 00:06:25.677
Sorry, Kenya. I'm the winner.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.972
It just means your

00:06:28.972 --> 00:06:32.183
Bible tennis beats Naniwa's Speed Star.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:36.813
Make it to the end for us, Shiraishi.

00:06:38.023 --> 00:06:39.232
Count on it.

00:07:04.716 --> 00:07:06.676
Kai-<i>kun</i>, you know what's coming.

00:07:17.187 --> 00:07:18.355
No luck, Captain Tezuka.

00:07:18.897 --> 00:07:21.149
Echizen's nowhere to be found.

00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:23.443
We couldn't find him either.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.945
Where'd that midget run off to?

00:07:26.821 --> 00:07:30.116
At this rate, he'll be disqualified
for not participating.

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:32.202
Echizen.

00:07:32.744 --> 00:07:33.787
That moron.

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:40.919
Did you check the bathroom?

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:43.713
Yeah, he wasn't there, but...

00:07:46.508 --> 00:07:48.259
Inui-<i>senpai </i>was...

00:07:48.551 --> 00:07:49.511
Inui?

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:51.346
"Inui"

00:07:51.346 --> 00:07:52.972
"Inui"
He says he's going to forfeit

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:55.058
"Inui"
because of a horrible stomach ache.

00:07:56.267 --> 00:08:04.484
Probability of poorly
prepared Inui Juice: 99.7%.

00:08:04.859 --> 00:08:11.533
Probability that the durian I consumed
last night was bad: 0.2%.

00:08:12.826 --> 00:08:15.704
Nucleotide!

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:19.958
Pitiful, Sadaharu.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:27.007
Begin the next match.

00:08:34.264 --> 00:08:37.851
Is this all the strongest
high schoolers can do?

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:45.525
How disappointing.

00:08:47.402 --> 00:08:48.570
Is that all you've got?

00:08:48.862 --> 00:08:49.529
Huh?

00:08:50.947 --> 00:08:53.658
I thought you would provide
more entertainment.

00:08:55.618 --> 00:08:59.372
You're not there yet.

00:09:01.249 --> 00:09:02.542
What are you talking about?

00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:05.879
You still have a long way to go, U-17!

00:09:18.641 --> 00:09:20.977
Wh-What was that?

00:09:20.977 --> 00:09:22.937
I didn't see anything.

00:09:28.902 --> 00:09:30.195
Interesting.

00:09:30.653 --> 00:09:33.198
They're finally taking it seriously.

00:09:35.116 --> 00:09:39.662
Super Ultra Great Delicious
Mountain Storm!

00:09:41.373 --> 00:09:43.833
Another Black Jack Knife?

00:09:43.833 --> 00:09:46.378
That blunt knife won't cut me!

00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:49.714
Black Tomahawk!

00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:02.060
If I can't cut you with a knife,
I'll split you with an axe.

00:10:51.609 --> 00:10:54.487
That was an interesting serve.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:03.955
What's wrong?

00:11:03.955 --> 00:11:06.499
That's not the serve I hit.

00:11:18.803 --> 00:11:20.972
Game and match, Akutagawa.

00:11:20.972 --> 00:11:22.098
Eleven-Nine.

00:11:24.351 --> 00:11:27.103
Kabaji, you need more practice.

00:11:30.732 --> 00:11:32.567
Game and match, Chinen.

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:34.778
Seventeen-fifteen.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.990
No!

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:41.618
I don't wanna go home yet!

00:11:45.497 --> 00:11:48.792
How filthy.

00:12:02.097 --> 00:12:05.266
Almost all the matches are over.

00:12:09.813 --> 00:12:11.398
Inui, are you okay?

00:12:11.731 --> 00:12:16.069
Yes. Probability of recovery: 100...

00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:19.280
...91%.

00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:23.076
Inui, have you seen Echizen?

00:12:23.076 --> 00:12:25.203
He's got a match to play,
but we can't find him anywhere.

00:12:25.578 --> 00:12:28.164
I haven't seen him.

00:12:28.623 --> 00:12:30.125
I guess it's the end of the line for him.

00:12:30.125 --> 00:12:33.128
Hey, what happened to that midget?

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.548
Did he run away with his
tail between his legs?

00:12:36.548 --> 00:12:40.010
Pretty pathetic for that big attitude.

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:41.553
Shut up!

00:12:41.553 --> 00:12:45.432
He'd never run from a match.

00:12:45.432 --> 00:12:49.686
Probability he has a reason: 100%.

00:12:50.228 --> 00:12:52.897
Take back what you said.

00:12:58.361 --> 00:13:01.156
But, Tezuka, he really will be...

00:13:03.908 --> 00:13:06.786
I'm gonna go look for him again.

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:08.288
Let me go with you.

00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:09.664
I'll go, too.

00:13:09.998 --> 00:13:12.334
I won't let that midget forfeit.

00:13:12.334 --> 00:13:14.961
Yeah. If we all look again,

00:13:14.961 --> 00:13:16.588
I'm sure we'll find him.

00:13:17.255 --> 00:13:22.510
Probability of finding Echizen: 97.3%.

00:13:26.973 --> 00:13:29.225
Everyone, find him.

00:13:46.242 --> 00:13:49.496
I can't believe Kirihara-<i>san </i>is so
helpless against his opponent.

00:13:49.746 --> 00:13:52.332
He's out of his league.

00:13:53.708 --> 00:13:56.378
That's one of the Rikkai Big Three,

00:13:56.836 --> 00:13:59.923
Renji Yanagi-<i>senpai</i>.

00:14:02.842 --> 00:14:03.677
I...

00:14:04.552 --> 00:14:07.972
I had decided I'd defeat
the three demons

00:14:07.972 --> 00:14:11.726
Captain Yukimura,
Vice Captain Sanada, and you,

00:14:11.726 --> 00:14:14.854
and become Rikkai's number one player.

00:14:15.438 --> 00:14:18.191
You're all about to graduate.

00:14:18.733 --> 00:14:20.193
I'm running out of time,

00:14:20.902 --> 00:14:22.237
so I...

00:14:24.614 --> 00:14:26.491
So I...

00:14:30.203 --> 00:14:32.580
I'll do anything!

00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:37.293
He's gone into Devil Mode!

00:14:37.711 --> 00:14:39.504
He's using a Knuckle Serve.

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.800
I'll paint you red!

00:14:45.176 --> 00:14:46.720
Four-zero: Yanagi.

00:14:49.597 --> 00:14:50.640
W-Wh--

00:14:51.016 --> 00:14:52.559
"Why?"

00:14:54.644 --> 00:14:56.563
That's what you'll ask.

00:15:05.905 --> 00:15:07.115
Five-zero: Yanagi.

00:15:08.283 --> 00:15:09.826
Six-zero: Yanagi.

00:15:10.493 --> 00:15:12.954
It's Yanagi-<i>senpai</i>'s match point.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:31.514
Renji.

00:15:36.811 --> 00:15:40.648
Referee, I, Renji Yanagi,
forfeit the match.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:44.527
What? He just needs one more point.

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:47.697
Don't be ridiculous!

00:15:47.697 --> 00:15:49.532
I'm just getting started!

00:15:49.532 --> 00:15:51.409
That's right.
You're just getting started.

00:15:53.411 --> 00:15:57.207
You will be the one
to remain at this camp.

00:16:05.757 --> 00:16:09.010
Climb even higher.

00:16:17.769 --> 00:16:19.646
I'll do it.

00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:23.024
Three-zero: Sengoku.

00:16:24.234 --> 00:16:26.820
Give it up already, Omoshiro-<i>kun</i>.

00:16:27.821 --> 00:16:32.492
That wasn't a hard hit,
and you couldn't return it.

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:35.870
Your wrists must still hurt.

00:16:36.663 --> 00:16:37.789
Sengoku-<i>san</i>.

00:16:38.248 --> 00:16:40.458
You shouldn't push yourself too hard,

00:16:41.001 --> 00:16:42.961
even though you're itching to play.

00:16:44.254 --> 00:16:46.381
Enough! I...

00:16:46.715 --> 00:16:47.424
Momo!

00:16:48.508 --> 00:16:51.845
If you destroy your wrists,
you'll have nothing left.

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:53.847
Fuji-<i>senpai</i>.

00:16:54.472 --> 00:16:56.266
Don't underestimate your injury.

00:16:56.725 --> 00:16:58.768
It'll be too late once
it becomes serious.

00:16:59.602 --> 00:17:02.772
But we made a promise.

00:17:03.231 --> 00:17:05.567
We promised the nine of
us would see this through.

00:17:06.943 --> 00:17:07.986
But...

00:17:08.653 --> 00:17:09.904
But...

00:17:09.904 --> 00:17:11.990
We'll all see it through in our own way.

00:17:14.117 --> 00:17:17.704
Momoshiro, see your way through tennis.

00:17:29.007 --> 00:17:30.925
Game and match, Akutsu.

00:17:30.925 --> 00:17:32.052
Seven-one.

00:17:35.138 --> 00:17:39.893
Akutsu-<i>senpai</i>'s become even stronger.

00:17:41.186 --> 00:17:42.020
Akutsu.

00:17:42.812 --> 00:17:47.400
Kawamura, I haven't taken away
your dream, have I?

00:17:47.776 --> 00:17:51.071
No. I'm bummed that I lost,
but I have no regrets

00:17:51.071 --> 00:17:55.033
playing against you at the end
of my middle school career.

00:17:56.743 --> 00:17:59.954
How naïve. Get out of here.

00:18:00.789 --> 00:18:06.002
I'm just here to return the
favor to your first year brat.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:14.427
Akutsu-<i>senpai</i>!

00:18:14.427 --> 00:18:15.804
It's Taichi!

00:18:15.804 --> 00:18:17.972
I brought you your charm!

00:18:17.972 --> 00:18:20.225
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:18:20.225 --> 00:18:23.311
If you make a scene,
they'll find out we snuck in here.

00:18:23.311 --> 00:18:24.270
Huh?

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:25.939
It's too big.

00:18:25.939 --> 00:18:27.273
Stand back.

00:18:31.945 --> 00:18:32.362
Hand it over.

00:18:32.362 --> 00:18:34.656
"Lucky Charm"
Hand it over.

00:18:35.865 --> 00:18:38.118
I'm glad I delivered it to him.

00:18:38.118 --> 00:18:39.828
There's nothing good about that.

00:18:40.245 --> 00:18:42.747
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:19:01.099 --> 00:19:03.768
You should see Coach Nyudo.

00:19:13.778 --> 00:19:16.031
How much longer are you
going to stand around?

00:19:16.656 --> 00:19:17.657
Right!

00:19:27.667 --> 00:19:28.293
This place...

00:19:29.919 --> 00:19:31.212
...is interesting.

00:19:33.173 --> 00:19:34.132
You're right.

00:19:37.093 --> 00:19:38.053
Well, then.

00:19:38.595 --> 00:19:42.140
I've got work to do,
so I'll leave the rest to you.

00:19:53.026 --> 00:19:55.779
The matches are over.

00:19:56.696 --> 00:19:58.948
Seishun Academy's Ryoma Echizen

00:19:58.948 --> 00:20:01.368
and Shitenhoji's Kintaro
Toyama are considered

00:20:01.368 --> 00:20:02.660
to have abandoned their match...

00:20:03.411 --> 00:20:04.579
...and are disqualified.

00:20:05.872 --> 00:20:09.292
No way! I'm sure that
midget will come back.

00:20:09.292 --> 00:20:10.919
Just wait a little longer.

00:20:10.919 --> 00:20:11.961
Please!

00:20:11.961 --> 00:20:13.129
No.

00:20:13.129 --> 00:20:15.465
We can't delay our schedule

00:20:15.465 --> 00:20:17.425
for some kids who left the court.

00:20:17.759 --> 00:20:18.885
Wait!

00:20:18.885 --> 00:20:20.011
Stop, Kikumaru.

00:20:20.929 --> 00:20:24.140
Why? If we don't do something, he'll...

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:26.685
This training camp wasn't made for us.

00:20:27.102 --> 00:20:27.769
But...

00:20:28.269 --> 00:20:30.438
Echizen broke the rules.

00:20:30.897 --> 00:20:34.150
It's unfortunate, but Tezuka's right.

00:20:38.863 --> 00:20:40.198
There's nothing we can do.

00:20:40.824 --> 00:20:42.826
What a letdown.

00:20:47.747 --> 00:20:50.458
Kin-<i>chan</i>, you idiot.

00:20:59.426 --> 00:21:02.262
You'll catch a cold sleeping out here.

00:21:03.096 --> 00:21:05.724
Oh, you're Coach...

00:21:06.516 --> 00:21:08.643
Yes, Saitoh.

00:21:09.144 --> 00:21:10.437
Let's go.

00:21:12.772 --> 00:21:14.441
Go where?

00:21:15.108 --> 00:21:16.526
To the main court?

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:18.111
No.

00:21:20.071 --> 00:21:22.907
Don't you want to become stronger?

00:21:29.873 --> 00:21:31.541
He said we'll get stronger!

00:21:31.958 --> 00:21:33.585
We've gotta go.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:18.064
"Preview"

00:23:18.064 --> 00:23:20.567
"Preview"
Hey, he said we'll get even stronger!

00:23:20.567 --> 00:23:20.942
Hey, he said we'll get even stronger!

00:23:20.942 --> 00:23:22.277
What are we going to do?

00:23:22.277 --> 00:23:22.944
Right.

00:23:22.944 --> 00:23:24.529
If you'd like to close the gap

00:23:24.529 --> 00:23:26.239
between yourselves and stronger players,

00:23:26.239 --> 00:23:28.908
try climbing this mountain.

00:23:28.908 --> 00:23:31.244
Will climbing a mountain
really make us stronger?

00:23:31.244 --> 00:23:33.038
Who knows?

00:23:33.038 --> 00:23:35.540
But nothing will happen
if you don't try.

00:23:35.874 --> 00:23:39.544
Whether or not you become
stronger is up to you.

00:23:42.213 --> 00:23:43.590
"Cliffs of the Heart"
The next episode of <i>Prince</i>
<i>of Tennis II </i>is: "Cliffs of the Heart."

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:47.136
"Cliffs of the Heart"
Really? Bring it on.
